    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_311d78f557a0c623fee16fecf4201e24ca761ca6c46208c8cc7d2c6ab19461dd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both sources support the same concrete PNT mechanism: the Euler-product logarithmic derivative encodes prime powers, nonvanishing on Re(s)=1 supplies boundary regularity apart from the pole at 1, and a Tauberian theorem transfers that analytic behavior to Chebyshev-function and prime-counting asymptotics.",
