    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3591d6233b8a30b6fec3294c45ebe3e6aad49155c408c9d6d9fa5dc0c7569a01",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Farey sources support two distinct discrepancy representations with a common arithmetic precursor, not one undifferentiated chain. Möbius inversion removes coprimality from Farey sums. For cumulative discrepancy, exact empirical-rank centering subtracts the triangular contribution and interval-length centering leaves an uncontrolled residue-class Möbius term. For quadratic Franel discrepancy, Bernoulli-Möbius coordinates and cyclic Dedekind-sum symmetrization lead instead to a gcd-weighted identity.",
