    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_40f650989903468b7a966252188a55083584692f3e61bf5b3d8b967c3911f33a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For an integrable positive random variable with survival function f, expectation gives the exact deterministic identity E[{X/t}]=-Pf(t). Independently, for a good kernel and after boundary and absolute-convergence obligations are discharged, the same Müntz sum-integral operator Pf has the pseudo-convolution representation with the fractional-part discrepancy kernel. Composing the identities turns a random dilation law into a deterministic convolutional object.",
