    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_679fe4b2d8ca9de0c8ec980ceedf3c1a97e6bd8988ca53182f6c09994e318d45",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The relation is a quantifier-level analogy between two concrete representations. For central zeta coefficients, saddle-point ratio control proves eventual Hermite behavior and hyperbolicity for each fixed Jensen degree, whereas the RH equivalence requires every degree and shift. For c_k, observed behavior can be governed by low on-line zeros while a hypothetical remote off-line zero may only become visible at an unbounded later index. Thus stable fixed local regimes do not discharge either universal criterion.",
