    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6b7e97f95bc2aca4632c6dcaf99f2e9c9c3a806b97585906c4620098392b31ee",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The sources give two concrete but inequivalent reciprocal-zeta representations. Mellin-Plancherel turns damped Nyman-Beurling sums into a zeta factor times a partial Möbius Dirichlet approximation to 1/zeta and a linear denominator. Separately, binomial differencing of the samples 1/zeta(2j+2) defines c_k, whose exponential generating function is e^xR(x)/x; the cited coefficient-growth theorem makes the c_k and Riesz growth criteria equivalent with the stated exponent shift.",
